# Local-only example for the Thrust Cloudflare root — never commit a resolved .env.
# CI uses protected GitHub environment variables/secrets instead; see README.md.
#
# <vault>/<item>/<field> are PER-OPERATOR placeholders (.claude/rules/security.md): copy this
# file to .env and resolve them to your own items. Do not commit a resolved reference.

# --- OpenTofu + scripts/store-tunnel-token.sh -------------------------------------------------
# On the Woven account this token needs:
#   - Account > Cloudflare Tunnel > Edit        (the tunnel object; Read is enough for the token fetch)
#   - the Workers VPC / connectivity-directory write permission, and the identity behind the
#     token must hold the account role "Connectivity Directory Admin"
# It must NOT be the terraform-r2-buckets token (that one only feeds the R2 state backend through
# the woven-r2-tofu AWS profile) and needs no Hyperdrive permission: this root never declares
# Hyperdrive, because the config's password would land in state.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
TF_VAR_cloudflare_account_id=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>

# --- scripts/hyperdrive.sh only -----------------------------------------------------------------
# A SEPARATE token with Account > Hyperdrive > Write (Read is enough for `check`), so the token
# that can edit tunnels cannot also rewrite database credentials. The script prefers this
# variable over CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. The wrangler OAuth login does not carry Hyperdrive.
HYPERDRIVE_API_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
